 "notes": "Limit on the electromagnetic gauge modulus d_e (Damour-Donoghue convention, L = kappa*phi*(de/4)F^2 with kappa=sqrt(4 pi G_N), Eq. 1) from Fig. 2(a) of the paper. Curve is the lower envelope of the paper's two observed 95% CL limits: H maser vs Si cavity (blue, ~1.5e-21 to ~1e-19 eV where it is lowest) and Sr clock vs Si cavity (red, dominant above ~1.5e-19 eV up to 4.5e-16 eV). Extracted from the vector paths of figure_2_v3.pdf in the arXiv e-print; the noisy spectral limit was reduced to a median per log-mass bin (85 bins), which stays within the width of the plotted band. The Sr/Si Projected (green dotted) sensitivity curve and the dynamical-decoupling high-frequency limits of Fig. 3 were excluded; the d_me limit (Fig. 2b, ScalarElectron) is a secondary result not reported here. Paper assumes phi is all of a local DM density of 0.3 GeV/cm^3 and applies the stochastic-amplitude treatment (limits already include the factor-3 rescaling per Centers et al.).",
